  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "bugfix",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Qwen3 previously left both GatedMLP dtype arguments unspecified. Its FP16 and EXL3 linear implementations consequently allocated half-precision down-projection outputs by default.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_0c4ce85b8954492ca2ec990ea9118ca8",
          "call_278afee1f4b545ed9c1848ae11e59367",
          "call_7605e834515c4971bdcb90fd12249388",
          "call_372af164fb49496eb99717b817c35b56"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The patch explicitly selects half-precision intermediates and float32 MLP output. This configures the down projection itself, rather than merely widening an already-rounded MLP result.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_24e5b1dd2c1e4ed7b8df3f7340552672",
          "call_278afee1f4b545ed9c1848ae11e59367",
          "call_dfca461cb9014d8aa09eb228e4b7d958",
          "call_7605e834515c4971bdcb90fd12249388"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A likely motivation is preserving down-projection range and precision without widening the larger gate/up intermediates. No inspected evidence identifies a specific failing prompt or measured accuracy improvement.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_24e5b1dd2c1e4ed7b8df3f7340552672",
          "call_278afee1f4b545ed9c1848ae11e59367"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "The change applies to every Qwen3 decoder MLP, including each down-projection slice. It does not change weights, dimensions, attention configuration, or the shared GatedMLP defaults for other architectures.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_24e5b1dd2c1e4ed7b8df3f7340552672",
          "call_0c4ce85b8954492ca2ec990ea9118ca8",
          "call_278afee1f4b545ed9c1848ae11e59367"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The earlier Qwen3 entry describes architecture registration and reuse of existing transformer modules; this change adjusts that builder's numerical policy.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_1e948be42a49415bbb730372bb668501"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #11, \u201cAssertionError: bias is wrong datatype,\u201d reports Qwen2 conversion failing on a bias assertion, followed by a reported fix. Its relationship here is only an inferred dtype-related comparison: its traceback names LinearEXL3, but the inspected parent already converts float bias to half, and this patch changes Qwen3 activation outputs instead.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_e53d840d93e546e6a37f6b05ab19d452",
          "call_372af164fb49496eb99717b817c35b56",
          "call_24e5b1dd2c1e4ed7b8df3f7340552672"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #29, \u201cAuto-YaRN for Qwen3? Maybe even set it dynamically?\u201d, concerns context-dependent RoPE scaling. The inferred connection is the shared Qwen3 identifier, not evidence that this MLP dtype change implements that request.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_9550b4795eef4ac4b9f5c568ac4034e8",
          "call_24e5b1dd2c1e4ed7b8df3f7340552672"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No model loading, inference, conversion, or GPU kernel execution was performed; native numerical behavior and performance remain unmeasured.",
      "Configuration inspection does not establish checkpoint compatibility, particularly for FP8 variants.",
      "The scalar check models storage and rounding only, not GEMM accumulation, activation kernels, or residual-add precision."
    ],
    "links": [
      "1db3dce033981fe2d1825165a9389b3fdcd21b67"
    ],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Qwen3 mixed-precision MLP output",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Qwen3Model now passes interm_dtype=torch.half and out_dtype=torch.float to GatedMLP. GatedMLP propagates the former to gate/up Linear objects and the latter to every down Linear. Forward computes SiLU(gate) \u00d7 up into the up buffer, projects down, and accumulates slice results before its final dtype conversion.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_24e5b1dd2c1e4ed7b8df3f7340552672",
              "call_278afee1f4b545ed9c1848ae11e59367"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Linear forwards its configured output dtype into both LinearFP16 and LinearEXL3 during loading and into LinearEXL3 during conversion. Both backends allocate their output using call override, configured dtype, then half as precedence. Thus the change affects the actual projection destination, including EXL3's reconstructed-weight and direct quantized paths.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_dfca461cb9014d8aa09eb228e4b7d958",
              "call_7605e834515c4971bdcb90fd12249388",
              "call_372af164fb49496eb99717b817c35b56"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "TransformerBlock supplies half-precision normalized MLP input, calls the MLP without an output override, and adds its result in place to the residual. The patch therefore widens the MLP result, not an explicit residual-buffer allocation; it does not establish that the entire block runs in float32.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_4bc99c1f5852446c90231cccde2e6df7",
              "call_24e5b1dd2c1e4ed7b8df3f7340552672"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B, Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B-Base, and Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B-FP8 each declare Qwen3ForCausalLM, SiLU, and hidden/intermediate dimensions 1024/3072. All three fit the unchanged MLP dimension mapping; the new activation dtypes are explicit builder choices, not their declared bfloat16 torch_dtype.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_a5cc24dc1fd745b8b3808dbece1f66a5",
              "call_7f2d474a3757418c94ff0acca726b4a1",
              "call_71aa39e7888949f5863cd4828560a9de",
              "call_0c4ce85b8954492ca2ec990ea9118ca8",
              "call_24e5b1dd2c1e4ed7b8df3f7340552672"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B-Base, and Qwen/Qwen3-1.7B-FP8 each declare Qwen3ForCausalLM, SiLU, bfloat16, and dimensions 2048/6144. The same dimension mapping and explicit activation policy apply to each.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_942c0acc57fd4693a9ba96729bcefb20",
              "call_10ff342471d4447fa642df05cd4d5698",
