          {
            "text": "Qwen/Qwen3-32B and Qwen/Qwen3-32B-FP8 each declare Qwen3ForCausalLM, SiLU, bfloat16, and dimensions 5120/25600. The same dimension mapping and explicit activation policy apply to both.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_6e026993522447c1b1c9696126846959",
              "call_34fdcb4e5332407d8cd5584fcdb34728",
              "call_24e5b1dd2c1e4ed7b8df3f7340552672",
              "call_0c4ce85b8954492ca2ec990ea9118ca8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library storage calculation gives float32 output bytes per token of 4096, 8192, 10240, 16384, and 20480 for hidden widths 1024, 2048, 2560, 4096, and 5120\u2014twice half storage. A scalar illustration rounds 2049 to 2048 in half but preserves 2049 in float32. These calculations illustrate the storage/precision tradeoff, not measured model behavior.",
